raw_response:
A shut mouth catches no flies is not about catching flies. Here are three plausible but wrong literal interpretations:

"flies" might just be insects; 
A person with a closed or "shut" mouth might be uninterested in eating or feeding any insects; 
A closed mouth could be seen as a sign of being asleep, so a mouth that is closed may not be able to "catch" any insects because the person is asleep.
